---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import TimeLine from "../components/cv/TimeLine.astro";
---

<BaseLayout sideBarActiveItemID="journey" title="Journey | Agueda Schwartz" description="From education research in Lima to building 0-to-1 AI products in the US. Career timeline, education, and certifications.">
  <div class="pb-8 mt-5">
    <div class="text-lg opacity-75">
      From education research in Lima to building 0-to-1 AI products in the US. Here's how I got here.
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="mb-10">
    <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold mb-5">Experience</div>

    <TimeLine
      title="Product Manager, WGU Labs"
      subtitle="Sep 2022 to Present | Remote"
    >
      The five-person team on a stalled AI portfolio was reassigned and I was told to carry it with AI instead, with fractional support from a UX researcher and an engineer. I built the operating system I ran it through on Claude Code and took the work from discovery to market validation, an evidence-based pivot, and a 12-week pilot with seven committed early adopters. I had written the go, pivot and kill criteria twelve days before the ads went live, which is what made the pivot call defensible when the data came back ambiguous. I also built a four-phase framework to structure the work and applied it honestly enough that it told me I had over-invested in research. Leadership wrapped the project in June 2026.
    </TimeLine>

    <TimeLine
      title="Senior to Lead Learning Experience Designer, WGU Labs"
      subtitle="Jun 2021 to Sep 2022 | Remote"
    >
      A public research university was moving its nursing programs to competency-based education and no one had mapped what that would actually require. I mapped all 93 courses in the BA and MA programs against a new national framework of ten domains, quantified the gaps, and designed the multi-month train-of-trainers series that carried about 40 faculty through the change. I also redesigned online modules and contributed to curriculum development across other partner engagements. Promoted from Senior to Lead in 15 months.
    </TimeLine>

    <TimeLine
      title="Learning and Development Specialist, Berdon LLP"
      subtitle="Jun 2020 to Jun 2021 | New York, NY"
    >
      A 200+ module professional education library used by senior accountants, partners and tax attorneys went out of date every year as tax law and firm policy changed. I owned the annual refresh and the standards it was held to, and I grew from supporting the subject-matter-expert partnerships to running them. I stood up LinkedIn Learning as a supplementary channel and contributed to a firm-wide CPE tracker that confirmed license renewals across internal training, external courses and LinkedIn Learning. I also led the firm's adoption of human-centered design with backing from the Director of L&D.
    </TimeLine>

    <TimeLine
      title="Product Owner, Innova Schools"
      subtitle="Nov 2017 to Jul 2018 | Lima, Peru"
    >
      Leadership asked for reporting dashboards. Talking to users showed me the problem was upstream, in how data got entered under deadline, so I cut the dashboard and shipped a data-entry tool that saved automatically and worked offline. Input errors fell 30% across 30,000 transactions and task time fell 10%, both measured at the end of the first cycle. With 2,000 people using the platform daily across 20+ school locations, I ran train-of-trainers through five people so the rollout did not depend on me being there.
    </TimeLine>

    <TimeLine
      title="Monitoring and Evaluation Manager, Innova Schools"
      subtitle="Mar 2016 to Oct 2017 | Lima, Peru"
    >
      Four learning platforms were running across 20+ school locations with no agreed way to judge them, including Khan Academy, an ESL platform, and a leadership and collaboration skills program. I designed the evaluations, tracking adoption, completion and frequency of use alongside learning outcomes, because usage is not comprehension. My recommendations were the primary evidence leadership used to decide what to scale network-wide and what to shut off. I also contributed to a multidisciplinary effort shaping a competency framework for teacher development.
    </TimeLine>

    <TimeLine
      title="Monitoring and Evaluation Coordinator, Innova Schools"
      subtitle="Mar 2014 to Feb 2016 | Lima, Peru"
    >
      There was no agreed methodology for assessing the network's innovation pilots. I helped a small team build one with learning outcomes as the primary criterion, and it became the starting point for the platform evaluations I would later own as Manager. I coordinated a team of data collectors in the field and led the qualitative research myself: observations, interviews and focus groups.
    </TimeLine>

    <TimeLine
      title="Research Assistant, Pontificia Universidad Católica del Perú"
      subtitle="Jul 2010 to Feb 2014 | Lima, Peru"
    >
      Conducted research on educational technology and digital learning resources.
    </TimeLine>
  </div>

  <div class="mb-10">
    <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold mb-5">Education</div>

    <TimeLine
      title="MA, Digital Media Design for Learning"
      subtitle="New York University | 2018 to 2020"
    >
      Digital media, instructional design, and learning science.
    </TimeLine>

    <TimeLine
      title="BA, Educational Psychology"
      subtitle="Pontificia Universidad Católica del Perú | 2005 to 2012"
    >
      Learning theory, cognitive science, and research methodology. The foundation for everything I build.
    </TimeLine>
  </div>

  <div class="mb-10">
    <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold mb-5">Certifications</div>

    <TimeLine
      title="Designing Strategy"
      subtitle="IDEO U | 2024"
    >
    </TimeLine>

    <TimeLine
      title="Designing a Business"
      subtitle="IDEO U | 2023"
    >
    </TimeLine>
  </div>

</BaseLayout>
